 Sovereign Intelligence alpha   step 4 of 9  plan
Here is exactly what changes, all inside your home folder:

~/.local/share/aienos/releases/alpha-20261026.3   this release, already unpacked and checked
~/.local/share/aienos/models/test-model
   the model: 0.0 GB in 2 files.
~/.local/share/aienos/engine.log   the engine's log, when it runs
~/.local/bin/aienos, the menu entry and the desktop icon (already there)

Not touched: NVIDIA's driver, the CUDA toolkit, libcuda, cuBLAS, /usr, /etc. No sudo.
Undo everything at any time:  aienos uninstall
Press Enter for the last question: 
 Sovereign Intelligence alpha   step 5 of 9  your yes
Type yes to begin. Anything else stops here, and nothing changes.
yes or no: 
 Sovereign Intelligence alpha   step 6 of 9  install
Checking every file of this release with SHA-256.
The hash runs in Omega (the sha256.om unit shipped beside me).

Meanwhile the user-space stack falls into the hole: libcuda, cuBLAS, nvcc.
That is the picture only. On disk those stay installed; AienOS just never loads them.

